    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084949": {
      "title": "Clinical Nurse Manager (CNM2) Research Nurse - ED Plus (0.8FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Clinical Nurse Manager (CNM2) Research Nurse - ED Plus (0.8FTE) Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Clinical Nurse Manager (CNM2) Research Nurse - ED Plus (0.8FTE) JOB SYNOPSIS We are seeking to appoint a dynamic nurse with excellent organisational, coordination, communication and interpersonal skills to promote and facilitate the conduct of a research project in the Emergency Department (ED) at University Hospital Limerick (UHL) and St James's Hospital |(SJH). The overall project focuses on the implementation of a model of integrated care for older adults who are discharged from the ED. The post holder will act as the person responsible for data collection and management for the randomised controlled trial across two sites, University Hospital Limerick and St James's Hospital. This post-holder will work closely with the Principal Investigator (PI) who is Co-Director of the Ageing Research Centre and the programme co-applicants/collaborators. The post holder will manage the day-to-day data collection of ED PLUS which include (but are not limited too), patient consenting, baseline, post-intervention and follow up data collection, tracking of deliverables relating to the recruitment and retention of patients, organisation of project meetings, as well as certain key dissemination activities. Faculty of Education & Health Sciences School of Allied Health Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: HSE Salary scales €64,579 - €78,404 (maximum starting salary €64,579) p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Rose Galvin School of Allied Health University of Limerick Email: rose.galvin@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Tuesday, 20th October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084949 Contact Number : Close Date : 20-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084749": {
      "title": "Digital Cultural Heritage Librarian (Re-advertisement)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Digital Cultural Heritage Librarian (Re-advertisement) Title of Post: Digital Cultural Heritage Librarian (Re-advertisement) JOB SYNOPSIS The University of Limerick Library is seeking an enthusiastic and innovative Digital Cultural Heritage Librarian (Assistant Librarian Grade I) to play a key role in developing and delivering the digitisation of digital cultural heritage collections, with a particular initial focus on the Bolton Library. Working within the Digital Scholarship and Systems team, under the guidance of the Digital Services Librarian, and in close partnership with Special Collections and Archives, this role will oversee digitisation and ensure that unique collections are discoverable, usable, and preserved for the long term. The role includes responsibility for supervising and supporting a small digitisation team and the successful candidate will have opportunities for professional development and to develop specialist expertise in digital cultural heritage, digitisation, metadata and digital preservation. The role holder will demonstrate strong professional judgement, effective people and project management skills, and the ability to contribute to service development while operating within an established strategic and reporting framework. Office of the Provost & Deputy President Library & Information Services Division Contract Type: Permanent Salary Scale: €47,176 - €72,821 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Ms Sinead Keogh Digital Services Librarian Library & Information Services Division University of Limerick Email: sinead.keogh@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Monday, 19th October 2026. Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Are you currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland? If you are not currently an EEA Citizen and have stated that you are currently legally entitled to work and reside in Ireland, you MUST upload a copy of your current Visa and Work permit in the attachments section application form. Unfortunately, if the attachment, as noted, is required and not provided your application cannot be processed. Please note your current work authorisation status must allow you to fulfil the terms of the contract on offer. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Staff Contact Email : Job ID : 084749 Contact Number : Close Date : 19-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084750": {
      "title": "PhD Opportunity in Circular Electronics and Automated Remanufacturing",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 PhD Opportunity in Circular Electronics and Automated Remanufacturing PhD Opportunity in Circular Electronics and Automated Remanufacturing (2 x Fully funded PhD positions available) Keywords: Eco-design for Remanufacturing, Automated Electronics Disassembly, Circular Economy & Sustainable Manufacturing, Refurbishment, Lifecycle Engineering, Industry 4.0 Supervisors: • Prof Eoin Hinchy, School of Engineering, University of Limerick. • Prof Eoin O’Connell, Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering, University of Limerick., • Prof Colin Fitzpatrick, Department of Electronic and Computer Engineering, University of Limerick. Overview: The ECODESIGN Doctoral Network (DN) is a pan-European research and training initiative aimed at developing the next generation of experts in sustainable product design and circular economy practices. It brings together nine leading universities and a range of industrial partners to train 15 doctoral candidates through interdisciplinary and intersectoral research. The programme is aligned with key EU policies, including the Ecodesign for Sustainable Products Regulation (ESPR) and the Circular Economy Action Plan, and seeks to strengthen European competitiveness, resilience, and sustainability. By adopting a holistic lifecycle perspective that integrates environmental, social, and economic considerations, ECODESIGN addresses the need for more sustainable and circular products across sectors such as electronics, automotive, and industrial systems. For informal enquiries please feel free to contact. Eoin Hinchy at eoin.hinchy@ul.ie or Eoin O’Connell eoin.oconnell@ul.ie Project description and role: The project is structured around five core pillars - Performance, Information, Planet, People, and Prosperity - delivered through dedicated work packages. It develops advanced ecodesign frameworks to support reuse, repair, remanufacturing, and recycling, enabled by Industry 5.0 technologies and human–robot collaboration. Key innovations include Digital Product Passports (DPPs) and data-driven tools to improve lifecycle transparency, alongside methods for assessing environmental, social, and economic impacts. Within this framework, the successful candidates will each undertake a PhD focused on eco-design for automated electronics remanufacturing, with particular emphasis on printed circuit boards (PCBs) or life consumption monitoring and DPPs. The roles will involve designing product architectures that enable efficient disassembly, testing, and reuse. The candidates will combine engineering design, automation, and sustainability assessment to develop practical tools and methods, working closely with international academic and industrial partners. Candidate Profile: We are seeking two highly motivated candidates with strong technical ability and an interest in ecodesign, circular electronics and sustainable manufacturing. Applicants should be keen to combine practical engineering with independent research and collaborate with international academic and industrial partners. Essential Requirements • Degree at National Framework of Qualifications (NFQ) Level 8 with first class honours (or equivalent), or a master’s degree in electronic engineering, Mechanical, Manufacturing Engineering, Mechatronics, Robotics, Computer Science, or a closely related discipline. • Strong interest in sustainable engineering and the circular economy, particularly in eco-design, remanufacturing, or electronics lifecycle management • Ability to work effectively as part of an interdisciplinary and international research team, engaging with both academic and industrial partners • Self-motivated, proactive, and capable of independent research, with excellent organisational, communication, and presentation skills • Excellent command of written and spoken English, demonstrated ability in technical writing, including preparation of reports, theses, or scientific publications • Knowledge and/or experience in two or more of the following areas: o Automation and robotics o Electronics or PCB design, testing, or manufacturing processes o Programming/software development skills o Digital manufacturing, Industry 4.0, or cyber-physical systems o Product design for disassembly, remanufacturing, or recycling o Data analysis, AI, or machine learning applied to engineering systems • Willingness to undertake international secondments with industrial partners Desirable Competences: • Track record of publications (preferably indexed in Web of Science) and/or conference presentations, demonstrating research excellence • Experience in electronics/PCB design, testing, or manufacturing processes • Experience with programming and/or AI/ML tools (e.g. Python, MATLAB, scikit-learn, TensorFlow) • Knowledge of eco-design, circular economy, or design for manufacturing and recycling principles Duration and funding • Marie Sklodowska-Curie Actions (MSCA) funded fellowship. • Tuition fees fully covered. • Funding for equipment, conference travel, and publications. • Duration: 36 months, full time • Expected start date for the positions: January 2027 Application procedure • Cover letter + Curriculum vitae • Details of two referees • Full academic transcript • Evidence of relevant project or research work Application End Date: Applications accepted via email to: Eoin.OConnell@ul.ie until 17:00 on October 30th 2026. Interviews will be carried out as soon as suitable candidates are identified. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084750 Close Date : 30-Oct-2026 17:00"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084829": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) in Digital Health",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/10/2026 Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) in Digital Health Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) in Digital Health JOB SYNOPSIS The University of Limerick invites applications for the position of Post Doctoral Researcher in Digital Health to support the evaluation of DASH, an innovative digital behaviour change intervention being delivered in partnership with the HSE. The successful candidate will work within a multidisciplinary team to design and deliver a mixed-methods evaluation, contributing to research in digital health, behaviour change, implementation science, and health services innovation. Faculty of Science & Engineering Department of Computer Science & Information Systems Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €47,273 - €53,925 (maximum starting salary €47,273) p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Katie Crowley Department of Computer Science & Information Systems University of Limerick Email: katie.crowley@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Monday, 12th October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. “This is a professional training and development role and the training and development relevant to this position will be completed within the period of the contract. Post Doctoral Researchers appointed will be expected to complete the Researcher Career Development Programme.” Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084829 Contact Number : Close Date : 12-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085009": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) Tourism Policy Data Analysis and Dashboard Development",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) Tourism Policy Data Analysis and Dashboard Development Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) Tourism Policy Data Analysis and Dashboard Development JOB SYNOPSIS The Post Doctoral Researcher appointed will be directed by the Principal Investigator - Professor Jim Deegan to undertake research at 7 tourism sites In County Clare to (a) Estimate the number of arrivals from the ticketing systems and to profile by demographic grouping such as Nationality/Age/Party Composition etc. (b) Design appropriate profiling questionnaires for the 7 sites, taking in to account the particular characteristics of each site; (c) Develop appropriate Wi Fi design questions that can be adopted and integrated to the triangulation of visitor profiling; (d) Develop a workable dashboard for each site once the various data exercises have been accomplished ;(e) Integrate the various dashboards in to on overall dashboard for the 7 tourism sites and (f) The researcher will also be integral to the production and development of a Tourism Barometer for the Cliffs of Moher Experience(Quarterly from late 2027) and latterly for the other 6 sites. By end of the project, it is hoped that an integrated tourism barometer for all 7 sites can be an achieved, but this will be subject to successful dashboard development at all 7 sites. Kemmy Business School Department of Economics Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €47,273 - €53,925 (maximum starting salary €47,273) p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Jim Deegan Director National Centre for Tourism Policy Studies Department of Economics. University of Limerick Email: jim.deegan@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Thursday, 22nd October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. “This is a professional training and development role and the training and development relevant to this position will be completed within the period of the contract. Post Doctoral Researchers appointed will be expected to complete the Researcher Career Development Programme.” Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 085009 Contact Number : Close Date : 22-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084929": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 2) in Agentic AI and Autonomous Network Optimisation (2 Positions)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/10/2026 Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 2) in Agentic AI and Autonomous Network Optimisation (2 Positions) Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 2) in Agentic AI and Autonomous Network Optimisation (2 Positions) JOB SYNOPSIS The University of Limerick invites applications for 2 Post Doctoral Researcher positions in Agentic Artificial Intelligence and Autonomous Network Optimisation on the RIASE project, funded by Lero in collaboration with Huawei Technologies. The researchers will develop intelligent agents that collaborate, verify recommendations and learn from experience to improve wireless network energy efficiency. The research combines large language models, multi-agent systems, reinforcement learning and knowledge evolution, evaluated using industry operational datasets. These positions offer an opportunity to advance autonomous decision-making through applied research with an industry partner. Applicants should hold a doctorate in a relevant discipline and demonstrate strong programming skills and research expertise in artificial intelligence, machine learning or related areas. Faculty of Science & Engineering Department of Electronics & Computer Engineering Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €55,399 - €60,250 p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Eoin O’Connell Department of Electronics & Computer Engineering University of Limerick Email: eoin.oconnell@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Tuesday, 13th October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. “This is a professional training and development role and the training and development relevant to this position will be completed within the period of the contract. Post Doctoral Researchers appointed will be expected to complete the Researcher Career Development Programme.” Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084929 Contact Number : Close Date : 13-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084809": {
      "title": "Research Assistant - Digital Pathology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/10/2026 Research Assistant - Digital Pathology Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Research Assistant - Digital Pathology JOB SYNOPSIS The Limerick Digital Cancer Research Centre (LDCRC), School of Medicine, University of Limerick, seeks a Research Assistant in Spatial Cancer Biology to support the development of advanced digital pathology capabilities using the Akoya Phenocycler-FUSION platform. The successful candidate will contribute to the establishment and validation of multiplex spatial biology and proteomic panels for cancer research, supporting innovative translational research projects and collaborations within LDCRC and beyond. Faculty of Education & Health Sciences School of Medicine Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €34,129 - €44,311 (maximum starting salary €37,173) p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Aedin Culhane School of Medicine University of Limerick Email: aedin.culhane@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Monday, 12th October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084809 Contact Number : Close Date : 12-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084989": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in Audio Perception and Gaming Performance",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Research Assistant in Audio Perception and Gaming Performance Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Research Assistant in Audio Perception and Gaming Performance JOB SYNOPSIS The University of Limerick is seeking a motivated Research Assistant to join a collaborative, industry-partnered project with Logitech. This role focuses on investigating the intersection of audio technology, human perception, and gaming performance. The successful candidate will design and conduct experimental studies, evaluate audio processing configurations (such as spatial audio and EQ), and analyse multimodal datasets to develop evidence-based recommendations for next-generation gaming audio. This is an excellent opportunity to work within an interdisciplinary team at the forefront of audio and human performance research. Faculty of Science & Engineering Department of Computer Science & Information Systems Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €34,129 - €44,311 (maximum starting salary €34,129) p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Fazilat Hojaji Department of Computer Science & Information Systems University of Limerick Email: Fazilat.Hojaji@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Friday, 23rd October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084989 Contact Number : Close Date : 23-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084869": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in General Practice (0.7FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/10/2026 Research Assistant in General Practice (0.7FTE) Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Research Assistant in General Practice (0.7FTE) JOB SYNOPSIS The University of Limerick is seeking to appoint a part-time (0.7 FTE) Research Assistant in General Practice in the School of Medicine This is an exceptional opportunity for a suitably qualified enthusiastic, dynamic individual with vision and experience to play a key role in the General Practice research programme. The successful applicant will work on a range of ongoing research projects as identified by the principal investigator. The successful candidate will need excellent communication, research and people skills. The current key research workstreams are based on the following topics: Rural healthcare, Medical Technology adoption, One Health and building healthcare capacity. This role it best suited to enthusiastic individuals who are adept at working both individually and collaboratively and ideally have strong skillset in communication, team-working, literature searching and review, qualitative interviews, quantitative surveys, quantitative and qualitative data analysis, and can contribute to research outputs and dissemination. Faculty of Education & Health Sciences School of Medicine Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €34,129 - €44,311 p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Liam Glynn School of Medicine University of Limerick Email: liam.glynn@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Tuesday, 13th October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084869 Contact Number : Close Date : 13-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084909": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in Intersectional EDI Practice (0.8FTE)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/10/2026 Research Assistant in Intersectional EDI Practice (0.8FTE) Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Research Assistant in Intersectional EDI Practice (0.8FTE) JOB SYNOPSIS The Department of Biological Sciences at the University of Limerick is seeking a Research Assistant to support Beyond Silver: Operationalising Intersectionality in Irish Higher Education, HEA-funded, cross-institutional project. The project aims to move beyond traditional, single-category approaches to equality, diversity and inclusion by developing practical, evidence-informed ways of embedding intersectionality within higher education policies, practices and institutional cultures. Working as part of a collaborative project team, the Research Assistant will contribute to research and literature reviews, stakeholder engagement, data collection and analysis, and the development, piloting and evaluation of practical resources for the higher education sector. The role will also support project documentation, reporting and dissemination. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to an innovative national initiative with the potential to inform meaningful and sustainable EDI practice across Irish higher education. This is a 0.8FTE position based at the University of Limerick. Faculty of Science & Engineering Department of Biological Sciences Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €34,129 - €44,311 (maximum starting salary €34,129) p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Audrey O’Grady Department of Biological Sciences University of Limerick Email: audrey.ogrady@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Thursday, 15th October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084909 Contact Number : Close Date : 15-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084969": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Student Evaluation of the Accuracy and Efficiency of LLM Generated Code",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Research Fellow - Student Evaluation of the Accuracy and Efficiency of LLM Generated Code Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Research Fellow - Student Evaluation of the Accuracy and Efficiency of LLM Generated Code JOB SYNOPSIS This research project focuses on software development using LLM-generated code. It will evaluate students’ ability to evaluate the correctness and computational efficiency of LLM-generated code, including whether more efficient solutions are more difficult to comprehend. Faculty of Science & Engineering Department of Computer Science & Information Systems Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €67,214 - €73,239 p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Michael English Department of Computer Science & Information Systems University of Limerick Email: michael.english@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Friday, 23rd October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 084969 Contact Number : Close Date : 23-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084449": {
      "title": "Vice President Innovation",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Vice President Innovation Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Vice President Innovation JOB SYNOPSIS University of Limerick seeks to appoint an outstanding leader who will drive innovation, industry engagement, entrepreneurship and commercialisation of research in line with the organisational strategic ambitions. This is a senior role requiring vision, a track-record of delivery and experience of establishing lasting partnerships with industry to drive world-leading innovation. The successful applicant will have experience of innovation, industry partnership in an academic environment with insights to lead knowledge transfer, commercialisation, new venture development, business engagement, academic programme development and consultancy services. Office of the Vice President Research Contract Type: 5 Year Fixed Term Salary Scale: €193,546 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Kevin Ryan Vice President Research University of Limerick E-mail: kevin.m.ryan@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Tuesday, 20th October 2026. Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Academic Contact Email : Job ID : 084449 Contact Number : Close Date : 20-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    }
